@@ -0,0 +1,115 @@
+# Demonstration guide
+
+## Project identity
+
+- Project: Personal Task Manager
+- Project Code: WST21-PM-2026-SF
+- Student Name: [LEAVE PLACEHOLDER FOR ME TO FILL IN]
+- Course & Year: [LEAVE PLACEHOLDER FOR ME TO FILL IN]
+- Database: SQLite
+- Practice repository: gwapo-proctor
+
+## What changed
+
+All Laravel files were moved from `task-manager/` into the repository root. Git history was retained. The two original README files were preserved under `docs/`, and the root README was rewritten for the assignment.
+
+| File | What to explain |
+| --- | --- |
+| `routes/web.php` | Named routes, HTTP methods, and controller actions |
+| `app/Http/Controllers/TaskController.php` | Validation, CRUD, status updates and redirect messages |
+| `app/Models/Task.php` | Eloquent model, allowed fields, statuses and date cast |
+| `database/migrations/2026_09_25_000000_create_tasks_table.php` | Tasks table columns and rollback |
+| `resources/views/layouts/app.blade.php` | Shared page structure and success/error messages |
+| `resources/views/tasks/index.blade.php` | Saved tasks, empty state, Edit/Delete/status controls |
+| `resources/views/tasks/create.blade.php` | Add Task form |
+| `resources/views/tasks/edit.blade.php` | Edit Task form and PUT method |
+| `resources/views/tasks/_form.blade.php` | Shared fields, CSRF, previous input and field errors |
+| `public/css/tasks.css` | Responsive layout and simple styling |
+| `.env.example` | Safe SQLite configuration with no real application key |
+| `scripts/setup.php` | Create environment/database, generate a missing key and migrate |
+| `composer.json` / `composer.lock` | Locked dependencies and setup/dev commands |
+| `database/factories/TaskFactory.php` | Task data used by automated tests |
+| `tests/Feature/TaskManagerTest.php` | Behavior and validation tests |
+| `tests/Feature/ExampleTest.php` | Starter homepage test now uses an isolated database |
+
+Laravel Boost was installed as a development dependency because the repository's existing agent instructions required it. It does not add a feature to the task manager.
+
+## How to start
+
+From the repository root:
+
+```bash
+composer run setup
+php artisan serve --host=0.0.0.0 --port=8000
+```
+
+Open http://localhost:8000 locally. In Codespaces, open port 8000 in the Ports panel. Its address is `https://YOUR-CODESPACE-NAME-8000.app.github.dev`; use the exact URL shown by Codespaces. Keep the forwarded port private.
+
+## Explain the MVC flow
+
+**Route → Controller → Model → Database → Blade**
+
+- **Route** receives the browser request and sends it to the appropriate controller.
+- **Controller** handles application logic, validates submitted data and communicates with the model.
+- **Model** represents Task data and communicates with the database through Eloquent.
+- **Database** stores the tasks in the SQLite file.
+- **Blade** displays the task data and forms to the user.
+
+On a write, the controller redirects after saving. The redirected list request then reads the database and renders Blade. This avoids resubmitting the previous form when the list is refreshed.
+
+## Explain each required feature
+
+1. **Add:** `create()` displays the form; POST `/tasks` calls `store()`. It validates the fields and uses `Task::create()` to insert a row.
+2. **View:** `index()` queries all tasks, newest first, and passes them to `tasks.index`.
+3. **Edit:** `edit()` loads the selected task into the form. PUT `/tasks/{task}` calls `update()`, validates and saves the changes.
+4. **Delete:** the form sends DELETE `/tasks/{task}` and `destroy()` deletes that record.
+5. **Update Status:** the button sends PATCH `/tasks/{task}/status` with the desired status. `updateStatus()` validates the status and updates only that field. Pressing the new button reverses the change.
+
+Laravel's route model binding finds a task from `{task}`. An unknown ID produces a 404. `@csrf` protects form submissions. `@method` lets POST forms express PUT, PATCH and DELETE. Blade's `{{ ... }}` escapes task text so it displays as text rather than HTML.
+
+## Suggested live demonstration
+
+1. Show the empty list and click Add Task.
+2. Enter a task name, optional description and due date. Save it.
+3. Show the saved task and success message.
+4. Edit the name and due date; save the changes.
+5. Mark Completed, then Mark Pending.
+6. Try an empty required field and explain validation.
+7. Delete the demonstration task and show the empty list again.
+8. Show `routes/web.php`, the controller, model, migration and Blade form in that order.
+
+## Commands used during implementation
+
+Equivalent ordinary terminal commands are listed below. On the local Windows build, PHP and Composer were invoked through downloaded portable runtime paths because they were not installed globally.
+
+```bash
+git clone https://github.com/vanarcaso/gwapo-proctor.git
+composer require laravel/boost --dev --no-interaction --prefer-dist
+php artisan boost:install --guidelines --no-interaction
+php artisan make:model Task --factory --no-interaction
+php artisan make:controller TaskController --no-interaction
+php artisan make:test TaskManagerTest --phpunit --no-interaction
+php scripts/setup.php
+composer run setup
+php artisan route:list --except-vendor
+php artisan test --compact
+composer validate
+composer check-platform-reqs
+php artisan serve --host=127.0.0.1 --port=8000 --no-reload
+```
+
+`scripts/setup.php` executed `php artisan config:clear`, `php artisan key:generate --no-interaction` when needed, and `php artisan migrate --no-interaction`. Laravel Pint formatted changed PHP files. Git status and staged diff checks were used before delivery. Files were moved and edited locally; no GitHub commit or push was made.
+
+## Verification
+
+- PHP 8.5.11; Laravel 13.33.0; SQLite.
+- 21 automated tests passed with 124 assertions.
+- All four migrations ran successfully, including the tasks migration.
+- Eight application routes resolve to `TaskController` methods.
+- Browser checks: empty list, add, saved task, edit, Pending → Completed → Pending.
+- Responsive check: 390px viewport has no horizontal overflow.
+- Live HTTP checks: list and CSS load, validation errors display, deletion succeeds, missing CSRF tokens are rejected on create/update/status/delete.
+- Re-running setup preserves the existing environment and reports no outstanding migrations.
+- Test-only task data was removed after checks.
+
+This is a single-user school demonstration with no authentication. No login, API, categories, search, notifications or other extra application features were added.
